-- ============================================================================
-- Migration: Sheet Metal Lookup Tables -- Manufacturability Severity (staging)
-- Purpose: Lands the "manufacturabilitySeverity" export (53 rows) -- the
--          real severity (Critical/Major/Minor) and, for several rules,
--          quantified per-material/per-thickness thresholds behind the 70
--          named DFM advice rules staged earlier (migration 483). Into the
--          same lossless staging table earlier Lookup Tables migrations
--          created. See migration 479's header for the staging/promotion
--          architecture.
--
--          NOT auto-promoted into dfm-scoring.service.ts -- see project
--          memory project_manufacturing_intelligence_data_reconciliation.md
--          for the full cross-reference. Headline finding: this export has
--          a REAL, per-material, per-thickness-bracket minimum bend-radius
--          factor table (InsufficientBendRadius rows, 10 material types x
--          up to 3 thickness brackets) -- e.g. Steel: 0.8x at <=6mm,
--          1.2x at <=12mm, 1.5x at <=25mm. This app's live, consumer-facing
--          DFM engine (dfm-scoring.service.ts) uses a single flat 0.8x
--          threshold for every material at every thickness -- meaning it
--          under-flags crack risk for anything thicker than the thinnest
--          bracket, for every material except mild steel. This is a real,
--          quantified, actionable gap -- but changing dfm-scoring.service.ts
--          changes live risk flags shown to users, so it needs explicit
--          sign-off before any code change, never a silent promotion here.
